# ── Docker build context excludes ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep host-only / platform-specific artifacts OUT of the image build context.
#
# Why this matters: Dockerfile.simple runs `npm ci` (stage 1) and `COPY . .`
# (stage 2). Without this file, `COPY frontend/ ./` would overlay the host's
# frontend/node_modules on top of the freshly installed, Linux/musl-correct
# dependencies — so Vite/Rollup would load the wrong-platform native binary and
# `npm run build` would fail with "Cannot find module @rollup/rollup-linux-*".

# Node dependencies & build output (reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Python bytecode & tooling caches
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
pytest-cache-files-*/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Version control & CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Secrets / local runtime config (provided at runtime via compose env)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local databases & data
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Logs & coverage
*.log
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
